{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":342006,"duration_api_ms":559553,"num_turns":9,"result":"\n\nNow I have a comprehensive understanding of the entire codebase. Let me construct the planning payload.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"problem_framing\": \"The tank simulation has ~18 state structs, ~70+ configurable kinetic parameters, ~15 hardcoded stoichiometric constants, 60+ invariant checks, and 19 integration test files — but the scientific meaning of fields, units, implicit assumptions, and known shortcuts is spread across code, TOML data files, and test assertions with no single reference document. Later refactor beads (B1/B2/B7 for unit taxonomy, C1 for mass conservation, D1/D2 for carbonate chemistry, E1/E4 for habitat ecology, G1 for parameter provenance) need one repo-local Rosetta stone they can cite when renaming fields, tightening invariants, or changing scenario expectations. The deliverable is docs/scientific_inventory.md with five required sections: pool catalog, rate/parameter catalog, invariant catalog, known nonphysical behaviors, and test dependency map.\",\n\n  \"assumptions_or_open_questions\": [\n    \"The bead shorthand references in the deliverable spec (A2, B1/B2/B7, C1, D1/D2, E1/E4, G1) map to tanksim-6e5.1.2, 6e5.2.1/2.2/2.7, 6e5.3.1, 6e5.4.1/4.2, 6e5.5.1/5.4, 6e5.7.1 respectively — the document should use both forms for clarity.\",\n    \"docs/scientific_specs.md already identifies 8 major scientific gaps with a v0.2–v0.5 roadmap. The inventory should reference but not duplicate that document; it catalogs what IS, not what SHOULD BE.\",\n    \"Some ProcessParams fields (respiration_dic_rate, photosynthesis_dic_rate) default to 0.0 in process.rs but are overridden to non-zero in data/process/default.toml — the inventory must note the effective runtime value, not just the struct default.\",\n    \"Monod half-saturation constants are named with _mg_total suffix but several are consumed as if they were concentrations (the core scientific bug). The inventory should flag this per-parameter without prescribing the fix (that's B1/B2's job).\",\n    \"The snapshot field names (e.g., nitrite_mg_l) imply mg-as-ion/L but the values are actually mg-N/L — the storage-vs-display ambiguity table must cover every such field explicitly.\",\n    \"Hardcoded constants like ALGAE_N_MG_PER_G_GROWTH=35.0 and ADULT_SHRIMP_BIOMASS_G=0.12 live in system .rs files, not in ProcessParams or TOML — the parameter catalog needs a 'hardcoded in source' location column.\",\n    \"The test dependency map must distinguish three categories: (a) bit-for-bit determinism locks (determinism.rs, save_load.rs), (b) numeric ratio/threshold assertions, and (c) qualitative ordering/direction checks — because category (a) breaks on ANY model change, (b) breaks on parameter tuning, and (c) should survive refactors.\",\n    \"EggCohort and StabilityTracker are internal bookkeeping structs that appear in save format — should they be cataloged as pools or as derived/transient state? Proposing: catalog them in pool table with a 'bookkeeping' compartment tag.\"\n  ],\n\n  \"proposed_work\": [\n    {\n      \"order\": 0,\n      \"summary\": \"Draft Section 1: Pool catalog table\",\n      \"details\": \"Build the pool catalog covering all stateful fields across WaterState (18 fields), SubstrateLayerState (9 fields), PlantGuildState (7 fields per guild), AlgaeState (3 fields), MicrobeState (5 fields), MicrofaunaState (2 fields), AnimalState (15+ fields including egg cohorts and stress accumulators), DetritusState (3 fields), FilterState (3 fields), HardwareState sub-structs (light/heater/filter/aeration ~15 fields), StabilityTracker (5 fields), EnvironmentState (3 fields), and TankGeometry (7 fields). Each row: field name | source file:line | unit (mg, meq, g, °C, index 0–1, count, etc.) | meaning (one-line scientific description) | compartment (water-column, substrate, biology, hardware, bookkeeping) | known shortcuts (e.g., 'total not concentration', 'fixed not habitat-scaled'). Add a sub-section on storage-vs-display: for every WaterState total that becomes a TankSnapshot per-liter field, list both names and note whether the display name implies ion-mass or element-mass units. Call out that all WaterState fields except temperature_c and ph are absolute totals (mg or meq), not concentrations.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"order\": 1,\n      \"summary\": \"Draft Section 2: Rate/parameter catalog table\",\n      \"details\": \"Catalog all ~70 ProcessParams fields from types/process.rs plus ~10 ShrimpRuntimeParams fields from types/biology.rs, plus all hardcoded constants from system files (ALGAE_N_MG_PER_G_GROWTH=35.0, ALGAE_P_MG_PER_G_GROWTH=5.0, PLANT_N_MG_PER_G_GROWTH=28.0, PLANT_P_MG_PER_G_GROWTH=4.0, FEED_P_TO_N_MASS_RATIO=0.10, ADULT_SHRIMP_BIOMASS_G=0.12, JUVENILE_SHRIMP_BIOMASS_G=0.05, o2_for_aob=3.43, o2_for_nob=1.14, juveniles_per_clutch=25, DO half-sat for decomposers=2.0, temperature Gaussian centers/sigmas, pH Gaussian centers/sigmas, photoperiod normalization divisors 9.0/10.0, plant shading bounds 0.2–0.7, nitrifier capacity 0.5g, etc.). Each row: parameter name | location (TOML path or source_file:line) | unit | implicit assumptions (e.g., 'uses total mg not mg/L', 'assumes 9h photoperiod is reference', 'fixed across all tank sizes') | volume/area/compartment-dependent? | downstream beads affected (B1/B2 for unit normalization, C1 for mass routing, D1/D2 for carbonate params, E1 for habitat scaling, G1 for provenance). Group by system: nitrogen cycle, plant growth, algae growth, dissolved oxygen, temperature, chemistry/pH, shrimp dynamics, microfauna.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"order\": 2,\n      \"summary\": \"Draft Section 3: Invariant catalog\",\n      \"details\": \"Document all constraints enforced by invariants.rs today: non-negativity checks on ~25 water/detritus/biology pools, [0,1] clamping on ~20 index fields, strict-positive geometry checks (4 fields), fill_height ≤ height physical constraint, berried_females ≤ adults clamping, empty egg-cohort cleanup, event_log cap at 200, non-negative process params (~10 checked), pH clamped [5.5, 8.5], temperature > 0. Then list MISSING invariants the vNext roadmap needs: mass conservation checks (total N, total P, total C across all pools should be tracked), concentration-based sanity bounds (e.g., TAN < 100 mg/L, DO ≤ saturation × 1.1), biomass carrying capacity enforcement (nitrifier biomass vs colonizable area), alkalinity-DIC consistency (pH should match carbonate equilibrium), stoichiometric balance validation (O2 consumed ≈ expected from nitrification + respiration), substrate nutrient non-creation (nutrients should only decrease unless replenished by detritus). Tag each missing invariant with the bead expected to add it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"order\": 3,\n      \"summary\": \"Draft Section 4: Known nonphysical behaviors / shortcuts\",\n      \"details\": \"Catalog each known shortcut with severity and owning bead/phase. Items to include: (1) Monod kinetics use absolute totals not concentrations — severity: scientifically wrong, owner: B2 tanksim-6e5.2.2. (2) Mass not conserved in shrimp/microfauna grazing — severity: scientifically wrong, owner: C1 tanksim-6e5.3.1. (3) pH solver is log-linear shortcut, not carbonate equilibrium — severity: scientifically wrong, owner: D2 tanksim-6e5.4.2. (4) Snapshot field names imply ion-mass but values are element-mass — severity: design debt, owner: B7 tanksim-6e5.2.7. (5) TDS/conductivity only sums 7 major ions — severity: cosmetic, owner: B7. (6) Biofilter capacity hardcoded at 0.5g regardless of media/flow — severity: design debt, owner: E1 tanksim-6e5.5.1. (7) Tank-size scaling incomplete for hardware and biomass — severity: design debt, owner: E1. (8) Plant trim always becomes in-tank detritus (no export) — severity: design debt, owner: C1. (9) No CO2 stripping from aeration — severity: scientifically wrong, owner: D2. (10) No denitrification in low-O2 substrate — severity: design debt, owner: E4 tanksim-6e5.5.4. (11) No chloride-modulated nitrite toxicity — severity: design debt, owner: F-phase. (12) No depth-based light attenuation — severity: cosmetic, owner: E-phase. (13) Photoperiod normalization differs between plants (10h) and algae (9h) with no justification — severity: cosmetic, owner: B2. (14) respiration_dic_rate and photosynthesis_dic_rate struct defaults are 0.0 (overridden in TOML) — severity: cosmetic, owner: D1. (15) Gaussian temperature/pH response curves are shared across all guilds — severity: design debt, owner: G1 tanksim-6e5.7.1.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"order\": 4,\n      \"summary\": \"Draft Section 5: Test dependency map\",\n      \"details\": \"Catalog all 19 tank_core test files and 2 tank_scenarios test files. For each test file, list: file name | what it tests | assertion type (deterministic-lock / numeric-threshold / qualitative-direction) | specific locked values if any | which model changes would break it. Key classifications: (a) DETERMINISTIC LOCKS — determinism.rs (full JSON equality over 720h), save_load.rs (roundtrip bit-equality) — break on ANY state field rename, default change, or arithmetic change. (b) NUMERIC THRESHOLDS — water_change_do_mixing.rs (1% relative error), water_change_mass_balance.rs (0.5% tolerance), tank_size_thermal_response.rs (5x concentration ratio), thermal_reproduction_penalty.rs (≥20% readiness gap), rooted_substrate_advantage.rs (≥15% biomass advantage), substrate_filter_integration.rs (≥10% detritus, ≥2% condition), cycling.rs (peak TAN >0.01, budget limiters to 1e-9), materialization.rs (geometry to f64::EPSILON), dissolved_oxygen.rs (DO convergence <0.25 mg/L). (c) QUALITATIVE DIRECTION — ambient_temperature_action.rs, filter_cleanliness_decay.rs, events.rs, chemistry.rs (pH direction), shrimp_population.rs (most assertions), plant_algae_integration.rs (most), overfeeding_effects.rs, end_to_end.rs (user journey). Note which tests should become qualitative envelope checks per the B3/B6 beads, especially determinism.rs which currently locks all floating-point values and will break on every parameter or formula change.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"order\": 5,\n      \"summary\": \"Add bead handoff cross-reference section\",\n      \"details\": \"Add a final section mapping each downstream bead to the inventory sections most relevant to it: A2 (tanksim-6e5.1.2 — save-schema migration): Section 1 pool catalog (field names that will change), Section 5 test map (determinism/save_load locks). B1 (tanksim-6e5.2.1 — unit taxonomy): Section 1 storage-vs-display table, Section 2 unit column, Section 4 items #1 and #4. B2 (tanksim-6e5.2.2 — concentration helpers): Section 2 parameters flagged as volume-dependent, Section 4 item #1. B7 (tanksim-6e5.2.7 — snapshot semantics): Section 1 storage-vs-display, Section 4 items #4 and #5. C1 (tanksim-6e5.3.1 — mass conservation): Section 2 stoichiometric constants, Section 3 missing conservation invariants, Section 4 items #2 and #8. D1/D2 (tanksim-6e5.4.1/4.2 — carbonate chemistry): Section 2 chemistry/pH parameters, Section 3 missing alkalinity-DIC invariant, Section 4 items #3 and #9. E1 (tanksim-6e5.5.1 — habitat registry): Section 1 substrate/filter pools, Section 2 biofilter capacity, Section 4 items #6 and #7. E4 (tanksim-6e5.5.4 — substrate redox): Section 1 substrate layers, Section 4 item #10. G1 (tanksim-6e5.7.1 — parameter provenance): Section 2 full parameter catalog, Section 2 hardcoded-vs-TOML location column.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"order\": 6,\n      \"summary\": \"Review, validate, and finalize the document\",\n      \"details\": \"Cross-check every pool and parameter entry against the actual source code to ensure no field is missed or mischaracterized. Verify that the invariant catalog matches invariants.rs line-by-line. Confirm that the test dependency map covers all test files in crates/tank_core/tests/ and crates/tank_scenarios/tests/. Ensure the storage-vs-display table covers all WaterState→TankSnapshot conversions. Check that severity ratings in Section 4 are consistent with the scientific_specs.md assessment. Verify bead ID references match the .beads/issues.jsonl backlog. Run a final pass for internal consistency (no contradictions between sections) and completeness against the acceptance criteria.\"\n    }\n  ],\n\n  \"readiness\": {\n    \"ready\": true,\n    \"risks\": [\n      \"ProcessParams struct defaults in types/process.rs may differ from runtime values loaded from data/process/default.toml — must verify effective values by reading both sources for every parameter.\",\n      \"Some hardcoded constants are defined as local variables inside function bodies (e.g., DO half-saturation of 2.0 for decomposers, capacity_g of 0.5 for biofilter maturity) and may be missed without line-by-line system file reading.\",\n      \"The determinism.rs test locks the entire simulation state as JSON — any field rename, reorder, or arithmetic change in the inventory document's recommendations could be misinterpreted as implementation guidance rather than cataloging, so the document must clearly distinguish 'what is' from 'what should be'.\",\n      \"The bead shorthand (A2, B1, etc.) is informal and not defined in any single authoritative source — cross-referencing with .beads/issues.jsonl is needed to ensure accuracy of the phase-letter to bead-ID mapping.\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"096133a8-6773-4a25-b224-3a09732e5008","total_cost_usd":1.4517563499999997,"usage":{"input_tokens":9434,"cache_creation_input_tokens":58962,"cache_read_input_tokens":232743,"output_tokens":6310,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":58962,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":414,"outputTokens":42798,"ca